{{also|Ignorant}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[ignoraunt]] {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|ignorant|lang=fro}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-ignorant.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{IPA|/ˈɪɡnəɹənt/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# [[unknowledgeable|Unknowledgeable]] or [[uneducated]]; characterized by [[ignorance]].
#* Tillotson
#*: He that doth not know those things which are of use for him to know, is but an '''ignorant''' man, whatever he may know besides.
#* Dryden
#*: '''Ignorant''' of guilt, I fear not shame.
# {{context|slang|lang=en}} [[ill-mannered|Ill-mannered]], [[crude]].
#: ''His manner was at best off-hand, at worst totally '''ignorant'''.''
# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} [[unknown]]; [[undiscovered]]
#* Shakespeare
#*: '''ignorant''' concealment
#* Shakespeare
#*: Alas, what '''ignorant''' sin have I committed?
# Resulting from ignorance; foolish; silly.
#* Shakespeare
#*: His shipping, / Poor '''ignorant''' baubles! &mdash; on our terrible seas, / Like eggshells moved.

